{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790283369,"nonce":"+82nKqipmZgSaJihztDxk0YV4AM=","message":"Answered 2026-09-24 (Luis), in the terminal renderer's key map; the issue stays closed. Design: doc/design/terminal-renderer.md.\n\n`y` yanks the id of the item under the cursor to the clipboard, in every view kind, over OSC 52. The escape sequence is why this needed no clipboard dependency and no daemon: it puts the id on the clipboard of whatever terminal is in front, including one on the far end of ssh, so an external chat session gets the reference by pasting.","files":null}]}